Subject: [PATCH] Passivo dry-run endpoint + report layer-of-block diagnostics
 (read-only)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

No behavior change to the gate; both additions are read-only.

- GET /api/internal/blog/passivo-consolidacao (dry-run): for every pair the gate
  would block, returns the plan WITHOUT writing anything — which post to keep,
  which to unpublish, the strength criterion (depth → age → cover → target_query),
  the three similarities (entity, title, semantic), and a `tipo`:
    * "reformulacao" (near-identical title) → suggested action 301;
    * "mesma-entidade-intencao-distinta" (group B: same entity, different intent
      like sintomas x tem cura x tratamento) → NOT unpublish (loses useful text);
      suggested action consolidate-or-keep, despublicar=null;
    * "reformulacao-semantica" (same idea, different words) → revisar.
  The apply step (unpublish + register 301) is deliberately NOT included: it waits
  on approval and on deciding the redirect mechanism (static host can't 301 from
  the Express app).

- Report diagnostics: each pair now carries disparoLexical/disparoSemantico so a
  merged pair that shows a low lexical similarity but blocks via cosine is no
  longer confusing (addresses the 0.575-with-bloquearia:true case).

Typecheck + build pass.

